	Well, I have sent out hack to a few people, but that turned out
to be only the first wave of the flood.  So, I am no longer mailing out the
source to the original hack (you hear malicious chuckling in the distance).

	But, you can still get both ibmhack.arc and arc500 (arc500.exe and
arc500.doc) by ftp from info-ibmpc at usc-isib.  Type "ftp usc-isib", and log
on as "anonymous" with password "guest".  Next, do a "cd info-ibmpc", and
set the file transfer type to tenex (type "tenex"), and "get" the files you
want - probably ibmhack.arc, arc500.exe, and arc500.doc.

	If you can't ftp usc-isib, DON'T PANIC.  Try sending mail to
info-ibmpc@usc-isib.  They are really nice people who would probably mail
the stuff to you.  They can also probably handle the deluge of mail better
than I can.  To be fair, if you have tried the above methods, and they don't
work, let me know and I will try to mail the stuff to you.

	Also, if you have mailed to me, and haven't got your own personal
copy of ibmhack.arc by the ethereal Jay Fenlason, it is because the name
server here at Berkeley has aphasia and can't figure out how to get the stuff
to your site - even return mail won't always get it there.

